# Verify UI (contract + live a11y)

When you **finish** any `apps/core` screen, overlay, or flow with **layout or copy** — or when the user reports a **visual/layout bug**:

## 1. Always (blocks “done”)

1. **`pnpm --filter @deelbaar/core lint`**
2. **Metro** — no `ERROR` / redbox / `Missing i18n path`
3. **i18n** — every `t('…')` in the diff exists in **`en`** and **`nl`** in `catalog.ts`

## 2. Layout (blocks “done”)

4. Read the **layout contract** for that screen under `docs/design/layout-contracts/` (or formulas in the task). If none exists for a new screen, add one before handoff.
5. **Prove invariants in code** — paste a **Layout proof** block (numbers from constants + `sheetTop` / `bottom` / heights). Cite constant names.
6. **One source of truth** — hero/sheet insets use shared derived constants, not conflicting magic numbers in the same feature.
7. Check [mobile-ux-master.md](../../docs/design/mobile-ux-master.md) and any pinned reference named in the task.

**Forbidden for layout pass:** lint only, file hash, “looks fine”, or guessing from chat without live evidence.

## 3. Live verify — agent-device (blocks “done” for design / UI bugs)

**No screenshots. No `capture-ui-review.ps1`. No PNG evidence pipeline.**

8. With Metro + Android emulator (or device) up: use **`agent-device`** to open the app, reach the target screen (press / deep-link), take an **accessibility snapshot**, and **assert** labels, roles, order, enabled state, and **rect sizes** (px→dp on Android) against the design/contract.
9. Emulator/Metro down → say blocked; **do not** claim visual pass; **do not** speculative UI patch.

```markdown
### Layout proof
- **Contract:** `docs/design/layout-contracts/<file>.md`
- **Formulas:** (e.g. H, R, bottom inset, pass/fail per row)

### Live a11y verify
- **Tool:** agent-device snapshot (interactive)
- **State:** screen + guest/signed-in
- **Asserts:** one line per criterion (label / size / order)
```

See [docs/design/agent-visual-verify.md](../../docs/design/agent-visual-verify.md) and speed rules in [docs/design/agent-device-fast.md](../../docs/design/agent-device-fast.md).

## Bug reports (“button too small”, spacing wrong)

1. **Forbidden:** UI edit from description alone.
2. **Before edit:** agent-device → snapshot → identify the node (tree order + rects) → prove cause in code.
3. **After edit:** re-snapshot + assert; layout proof if spacing.

## When this applies

Screens, modals, sheets, carousels, auth, tab chrome, visible copy changes.

**Not required:** logic-only, API, types, config with no UI surface.
